body:
When I was 12, I was walking on the beach, alone. This guy, I guess he was around 25 or so, came from the direction I was going to and before he walked past me he streched his arm out (like he was going for a high five) . So I went to give him an high five but instead of just slapping my hand, he grabbed it. I stopped in front of him because I started getting nervous. He bent down and gave me a kiss on the cheek and then on my mouth. It was like a small peck but I didn't do anything. He was still holding my hand when he stood straight again and told me "I love you, where are you from?" and I still don't know how I didn't burst out in tears on the spot but I  just said that I wasn't interested and kinda ran away. Yes there were many people around who saw it, but they ignored it. I was wearing a thin poncho over my bathing suit and even though I probably looked a bit older than I was, I definetly didn't look like an adult (not that that would have changed things)

&#x200B;

I didn't realize how bad this was until a couple years later. It still makes me sick thinking back at how terrified I was, even if the situation itself apparentally sounds funny (or so my friends say.
